  "knowledgePattern": "Eliminate the AP part with successive differences",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Write one formula for each total",
      "body": "<p>Write <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>, where a and d describe the AP, and b and r describe the GP.</p>",
      "recap": "The two sequences need separate first terms.",
      "pitfall": "The question asks for the GP’s sum, not the combined sequence’s sum.",
      "pause": "Use n=1,2,3,4 to write four equations.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l10",
          "reminder": "Match the stated AP and GP term positions before using a sum formula."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Subtract twice",
      "body": "<p>Subtract each equation from the next to remove a. Then subtract neighbouring new equations to remove d.</p>",
      "recap": "An AP has constant first differences, so its second differences are zero.",
      "pitfall": "Keep the same subtraction order throughout.",
      "pause": "Use the two remaining equations to find r and b, then sum the GP.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l09",
          "reminder": "Use b/(1−r) only after checking |r|<1."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p><strong>1.</strong> Write <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x0007C;</mo><mo>&#x0003C;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>. The first differences from the data are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></math>. Their successive differences are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>2.</strong> The AP contribution disappears in a second difference. Algebraically these two differences are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>b</mi><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math>. The first is nonzero, so their ratio gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>3.</strong> Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>, so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></math>. The infinite GP sum is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></math>, answer B.</p><p><strong>4.</strong> For an independent check, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math> together with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math> reproduce all four stated totals. The convergence requirement is satisfied.</p>"
